<title>USA: CHESS-Moves in Game Two of Kasparov vs. Deep Blue.</title>
<headline>CHESS-Moves in Game Two of Kasparov vs. Deep Blue.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are the moves in Sunday's second game of the $1.1 million six-game re-match between world chess champion Garry Kasparov and the IBM supercomputer Deep Blue.</p>
<p>Ruy Lopez Opening (also known as Spanish game)</p>
<p>    Deep Blue (white)   Kasparov (black)</p>
<p>    1.  e4		  e5</p>
<p>    2.  Nf3		 Nc6</p>
<p>    3.  Bb5		 a6</p>
<p>    4.  Ba4		 Nf6</p>
<p>    5.  O-O		 Be7</p>
<p>    6.  Re1		 b5</p>
<p>    7.  Bb3		 d6</p>
<p>    8.  c3		  O-O</p>
<p>    9.  h3		  h6</p>
<p>    10. d4		  Re8</p>
<p>    11. Nbd2		Bf8</p>
<p>    12. Nf1		 Bd7</p>
<p>    13. Ng3		 Na5</p>
<p>    14. Bc2		 c5</p>
<p>    15. b3		  Nc6</p>
<p>    16. d5		  Ne7</p>
<p>    17. Be3		 Ng6</p>
<p>    18. Qd2		 Nh7</p>
<p>    19. a4		  Nh4</p>
<p>    20. Nxh4		Qxh4</p>
<p>    21. Qe2		 Qd8</p>
<p>    22. b4		  Qc7</p>
<p>    23. Rec1		c4</p>
<p>    24. Ra3		 Rec8</p>
<p>    25. Rca1		Qd8</p>
<p>    26. f4		  Nf6</p>
<p>    27. fxe5		dxe5</p>
<p>    28. Qf1		 Ne8</p>
<p>    29. Qf2		 Nd6</p>
<p>    30. Bb6		 Qe8</p>
<p>    31. R3a2		Be7</p>
<p>    32. Bc5		 Bf8</p>
<p>    33. Nf5		 Bxf5</p>
<p>    34. exf5		f6</p>
<p>    35. Bxd6		Bxd6</p>
